# Tsakos Energy Navigation (TEN / NYSE:TEN) fleet manifest — METHODOLOGY §4.1, §11.6
# SHADOW DRAFT 2026-09-11 (ten.yaml.draft — invisible to the loader; consumed only by
# scripts/shadow_regen.sh, which copies it over ten.yaml inside a detached worktree
# next to inputs/balance_sheets/ten_2026-Q2.yaml.draft). Record:
# decisions/ten_shadow_build_2026-09-11.md.
# Source: the 2026-Q1 live manifest (TEN Data Kit May 11, 2026; June 5, 2026 kit
# reconcile 2026-06-11; Q1 2026 6-K filed 2026-05-22; the 2026-07-15 reconciliation,
# decisions/ten_reconciliation_prereg_2026-07-15.md) rolled to 2026-06-30 on the
# TEN H1/Q2 2026 results release, GlobeNewswire 3359616, 2026-09-10 ("TEN, Ltd.
# Reports Profits for the First Half and Second Quarter of 2026"; saved as
# inputs/research_issuer/ten/2026-09-10_ten_h1_2026_results_pr.txt). The release
# carries NO per-vessel fleet table — only FLEET DATA aggregates ("Number of
# vessels at end of period 64.0", "Dwt at end of period (in thousands) 7,702",
# "Average age of fleet at end of period (years) 10.5") and the 26-row newbuilding
# table — so every row below is its Q1 row with the age rolled +0.25 (91/365 y,
# 2026-03-31 -> 2026-06-30); per-vessel EMPLOYMENT at 6/30 is UNVERIFIED (shadow)
# throughout (the H1-2025 6-K carried no fleet table either — plan on the data kit
# at the live land). Ages in this file are NOT a sourced hull list for 6/30.
# Balance sheet date: 2026-06-30.
#
# SUBSEQUENT-EVENTS AUDIT FIRST (release SUBSEQUENT EVENTS / CORPORATE AFFAIRS,
# 2026-09-10) — what is IN and OUT of the 2026-06-30 snapshot:
#   IN  — Ulysses (2016-built VLCC): Q1 6-K ex 99.1 SUBSEQUENT EVENTS "On May 20,
#         2026, the Company completed the sale of a 10-year-old VLCC ... about
#         $83 million in free cash after repayment of existing debt" (vessel
#         unnamed there); identity per 20-F Note 17(c) (MOA 2026-01-22, VLCC
#         Ulysses) + release CORPORATE STRATEGY "2016-built VLCC Ulysses";
#         release Q2 "Gain on sale of vessels (37,870)" -> GONE from the fleet:
#         no row, and no longer held-for-sale inside the WC composite.
#   OUT — Anfield DP: "on July 28, 2026, TEN took delivery of the DP2 suezmax
#         shuttle tanker Anfield DP from Samsung Heavy Industries" -> a NEWBUILD
#         at 6/30 (advances on the sheet); joins the off-curve shuttle book at
#         the Q3 refresh. Not a row (no Shuttle class exists on a curve anyway).
#   OUT — Alaska + Archangel: "in August 2026 TEN concluded the sale of two
#         2006-built suezmax tankers, the Alaska and Archangel, for net proceeds
#         of $100 million" -> OWNED at 6/30, rows STAY; they leave at Q3.
#         Held-for-sale AT 6/30? Release silent -> JUDGMENT CALL (the
#         NON-conservative side taken, exposure bounded), see their rows.
#   OUT — July 2026 "$1.00 per share" dividend; Series E call intent (May 28,
#         2027); LNG newbuild row 26 firm-up (undated in the release).
#   UNVERIFIED (shadow) — Arctic + Antarctic (2007-built Suezmaxes): OUT here is
#         the CONSERVATIVE DEFAULT, NOT a prior state. The five-year SLB
#         "commenced" 2021-06-21 (20-F leases note) -> term ENDED 2026-06-21,
#         BEFORE the snapshot; repurchase agreed 2026-04-07 (Q1 6-K ex 99.1
#         SUBSEQUENT EVENTS: "agreed to repurchase two of its 2007-built suezmax
#         tankers, currently operating under five-year leases at prices below
#         current fair market value"); the pair was still operated at 6/30
#         (release dwt 7,702k = the Jun-5 kit's 63 hulls INCLUDING them;
#         Antarctic on TC to Dec-26 per the 20-F fleet table). No source on disk
#         dates the COMPLETION -> excluded (chartered-in); re-add as OWNED only
#         on the 6-K leases / vessels note. If it flips, NAV here is UNDERSTATED
#         (the likeliest 6-K resolution, direction +): 56 -> 58, crude 37 -> 39,
#         Suezmax 14 -> 16 in the same edit. Indicators (inference, not
#         disclosure) are listed at the Suezmax 2006-2007 cohort comment.
#
# Scope = the **56 on-curve OWNED in-water vessels** as of 2026-06-30 — the SAME
# 56 hulls as the reconciled 2026-Q1 manifest (no sourced addition or removal
# dated inside Q2):
#   - Crude: 2 VLCC + 14 conventional Suezmax + 21 Aframax = 37 vessels
#   - Product: 4 Aframax LR + 9 Panamax LR1 + 2 MR + 2 Handysize = 17 vessels
#   - LNG: 2 LNG carriers = 2 vessels
#   - Shuttle: **EXCLUDED** (4 in-water DP2 shuttle tankers — Brasil 2014, Rio 2016,
#     Athens 04, Paris 24 — handled OFF-CURVE via `shuttle_contracted_book`
#     per METHODOLOGY §11.6, NOT in this manifest; Anfield DP, delivered
#     2026-07-28, becomes the 5th from Q3)
#   - CHARTERED-IN, NOT OWNED on this build (excluded from NAV per the 2343/CMDB
#     convention; ASC 842 true-sale SLBs, 20-F leases note): Sakura Princess
#     (SLB Dec-2020, extended to ~Dec-2026) and — as the CONSERVATIVE DEFAULT,
#     not a prior state — Arctic + Antarctic (SLB term ended 2026-06-21;
#     repurchase agreed 2026-04-07; completion UNVERIFIED (shadow), see above).
#   - HELD FOR SALE at 6/30: NONE under the judgment call taken (Ulysses sold
#     May-20-2026; Alaska + Archangel carried as owned-and-operating at 6/30 —
#     their HFS status at 6/30 is UNVERIFIED (shadow), see their rows).
#
# Total in-water fleet at 2026-06-30 = 63 OPERATED vessels on this build
# (56 owned on-curve + 4 shuttle off-curve + 3 chartered-in) — the Q1 64 less
# Ulysses. The release prints "Number of vessels at end of period 64.0", but its
# "Dwt at end of period (in thousands) 7,702" equals the Jun-5 kit's 63 in-water
# hulls / 7,701,519 DWT, the Q1 6-K ex 99.1 printed 64.0 / 8,003k at Mar-31 (the
# −301k delta is one VLCC), and "Average number of vessels during period 63.5"
# (Q2 and H1) fits 63 at period-end — a 64th hull at 6/30 is unsupported by the
# release's own dwt/average series (decisions/ten_h1_release_check_2026-09-10.md
# §4). Unresolved until a fleet list; NO hull is added on the printed 64.0.
#
# Newbuild orderbook at 2026-06-30 = 19 hulls, handled via balance sheet
# `newbuild_capex_commitments` (0, convention) + `newbuild_advances_paid`
# (470,050 $K, release BALANCE SHEET DATA "Advances for vessels under
# construction") — no NB rows, no years_to_delivery (OFF_CONVENTION advances-only):
#   - 10 DP2 Shuttle Suezmaxes (Anfield DP + HN2733-2741): contract value ~$1,481M
#     (Anfield DP delivered 2026-07-28 -> 9 remain at the release date; release:
#     "the third in a series of 12 DP2 shuttle tankers under construction at that
#     yard" = Athens 04 + Paris 24 + Anfield DP + 9)
#   - 5 Panamax LR1 (Hull 1623, 0307383-86): contract value ~$280M
#   - 3 VLCC (HN5331, 5332, 5335): contract value ~$385M
#   - 1 LNG carrier (HN3643, 81,755 DWT): contract value ~$254M
#   - NOT counted: the second LNG carrier — release "TEN's CURRENT NEWBUILDING
#     PROGRAM" row 26 "TBN | LNG Carrier | Q1 2029 | Under Construction | TBA"
#     (an "Optional Vessel" in the Q1 6-K ex 99.1 table) is undated in the
#     release; MB LNG Weekly 29 (2026-07-16) would place the firm-up after 6/30
#     -> UNVERIFIED (shadow): awaits the 6-K Subsequent Events note. No price
#     disclosed (NEWBUILD_PRICE_PENDING).
#   Release delivery schedule (2026-09-10, "Delivery (exp)"): LR1 AMAZONA Q2-27,
#   TBN Q3-27, TBN Q4-27, TBN Q3-28, TBN Q3-28; VLCC CHAIRMAN DJS Q4-27, TBN
#   Q1-28, TBN Q2-28; DP2 ARIANO SUASSUNA Q3-27, ELZA SOARES Q4-27, MARIA FIRMINA
#   Q1-28, CAROLINA DE JESUS Q2-28, IPANEMAS Q3-28, MARACANA Q3-28, CORINTHIANS
#   Q4-28, DR SOCRATES Q4-28, TBN Q4-28; LNG NY KNICKS Q3-28, TBN Q1-29. All 9
#   undelivered shuttle hulls carry Employment "Yes"; LR1 / VLCC / LNG "TBA".
#   The table has no contract prices, dwt, or commitment schedule.
#
# TEN is the first **3-sleeve hybrid** on the watchlist (`THREE_SLEEVE_TICKERS`)
# — the carve-out routes (crude_carve_out + product_carve_out + lng_carve_out)
# all run against the same fleet manifest, with vessel.sleeve / class driving
# the split. The shuttle sleeve sits at the corporate level via
# `shuttle_contracted_book` (METHODOLOGY §11.6, off-curve-at-contracted-book).
#
# Vessel ages computed from build year/month to 2026-06-30: each 2026-Q1 age (to
# 2026-03-31) rolled +0.25 (91/365 y), two decimals kept — no hull re-dated, no
# build month re-sourced. Eco = built post-2014 per §3.1 definition. Scrubber flags
# reflect data kit "scrubber-fitted" callouts, UNCHANGED (the same 9 operating
# scrubber:true rows as Q1; OPERATING_SCRUBBER_QUEUE posture unchanged); default
# false when unspecified.
# Employment fields (charter_status / charter_rate) are the Q1 values throughout:
# the release has no per-vessel employment, and the Jun-5 kit's Q2 deltas
# (ten_log 2026-06-11 "Vintage deltas — DOCUMENTED, not applied": Sola TS
# $25,651 -> $26,651 from May-1-2026; Dimitris P spot -> TC $40,000 min; Alaska +
# Archangel fixed -> spot-indexed TCs; Hercules I $140,000 unchanged to Nov-26)
# are NOT applied in the shadow. The reason is ATTRIBUTION, not provenance: the
# kit deltas are dated BEFORE the snapshot and the ten_log 2026-06-11 entry is a
# dated reference the provenance guard accepts, but applying them here would
# fold a strip-only change into the balance-sheet-swap attribution. Direction:
# the kept Q1 rates OVERSTATE the Suezmax TC leg (Archangel 102,000 fixed vs a
# spot-indexed TC) and understate Sola TS by $1,000/day. Apply at the live land
# (charter_status spot for Alaska/Archangel; Sola TS 26651; Dimitris P TC
# 40000) and re-derive spot_coverage_pct from the rows. Flagged per row as
# UNVERIFIED (shadow) — a live-land decision.

