  # 2006-2007 ice-class 1A cohort (older but specialized; treat as ice-class premium implicit in TC rate)
  # Antarctic + Arctic (2007-built) — NO ROWS on this build: OUT is the CONSERVATIVE
  # DEFAULT, NOT a prior state (verifier 2026-09-11). 20-F leases note: "On June
  # 21, 2021, the Company commenced a new five-year sale and leaseback agreement
  # for each of the two suezmaxes, Arctic and Antarctic" (net sale price
  # $52,304K; ASC 842 TRUE SALE; weighted-average remaining term 0.48y at
  # Dec-31-2025) -> the term ENDED 2026-06-21, BEFORE the snapshot. Q1 6-K ex
  # 99.1 SUBSEQUENT EVENTS: "On April 7, 2026, TEN agreed to repurchase two of
  # its 2007-built suezmax tankers, currently operating under five-year leases
  # at prices below current fair market value". Still operated at 6/30: release
  # dwt 7,702k ties to the Jun-5 kit's 63 hulls INCLUDING them (ten_log
  # 2026-06-11); Antarctic on TC to Dec-26 (20-F fleet table). COMPLETION is in
  # no source on disk (the release has no "Arctic" / "Antarctic" / "repurchase"
  # text) -> excluded. Circumstantial ONLY (release 2026-09-10; inference, not
  # disclosure): Charter hire expense Q2 2,646 vs Q1 3,386 (Q1 6-K ex 99.1) vs
  # Q2-2025 3,321 — at the logged bareboat rates ($13,870/day each; ten_log
  # 2026-06-11) the pair fits on hire for roughly 60 of 91 days, i.e. leases
  # ending late May / early June 2026; Vessels, net +10,118 net of 46,295 D&A
  # with no NB delivery; Q2 D&A 46,295 vs Q1 44,147 with Ulysses gone; Q2
  # investing +3,763 after the VLCC proceeds — all consistent with the leases
  # ending inside Q2 and the repurchase completing before 6/30. NOT a citation
  # for ownership; re-add ONLY on the 6-K leases / vessels note. If it flips:
  # NAV UNDERSTATED here (cash already net of the repurchase price; two
  # 2007-built Suezmax marks missing) — the likeliest 6-K resolution, direction
  # +: on_curve_total 56 -> 58, crude_sleeve_count 37 -> 39, Suezmax 14 -> 16,
  # in the same edit. UNVERIFIED (shadow): awaits the 6-K leases / vessels note.
  # Alaska + Archangel (2006-built, the 2024 buy-backs): OWNED AT 6/30 — sold
  # AFTER the snapshot: "in August 2026 TEN concluded the sale of two 2006-built
  # suezmax tankers, the Alaska and Archangel, for net proceeds of $100 million"
  # (release SUBSEQUENT EVENTS, 2026-09-10). Aggregate + net, never split — NOT
  # promotable, do not back-solve per hull. Rows stay; they leave at Q3.
  # JUDGMENT CALL (shadow) — held-for-sale AT 6/30? The release has no "held for
  # sale" / MOA text and no held-for-sale balance-sheet line. TAKEN: NOT
  # held-for-sale at 6/30 -> ON-CURVE here. This is the NON-CONSERVATIVE side
  # (verifier 2026-09-11): if the pair was HFS at 6/30 its carrying value
  # already sits inside Other assets 286,240 (the Ulysses precedent) and these
  # two on-curve marks double-count it. Why taken: (i) no MOA date exists for
  # this pair in any source on disk — the 9/01 PR (GlobeNewswire 3354219,
  # inputs/earnings_calendar.yaml TEN basis; text not on disk, ten_log entry
  # owed; WebFetch 2026-09-11 reads only "TEN announced today the sale of two
  # 2006-built Suezmax tankers. This transaction will release in excess of
  # $100 million to the company's cash reserves" — no agreement date, neither
  # "agreed" nor "concluded") and the 9/10 release (SUBSEQUENT EVENTS: "in
  # August 2026 TEN concluded the sale") both post-date the quarter; under
  # ASC 360-10-45-9 a
  # signed MOA normally meets the held-for-sale criteria, but TEN discloses no
  # classification policy (20-F Note 17(c) says only that an MOA was signed for
  # Ulysses; the Ulysses HFS-at-Mar-31 treatment was the Q1 prereg's inference
  # from the Other-assets swing, not a disclosed policy); (ii) the release's
  # Vessels, net bridge (3,145,164 -> 3,155,282, +10,118, net of 46,295 D&A and
  # no NB delivery) is NON-DISCRIMINATING: a 6/30 HFS reclass of two
  # 20-year-old hulls would move only their (undisclosed, small) carrying value
  # — not the $100M net proceeds — and the unidentified Q2 additions of roughly
  # $52-56M have a named candidate (the Apr-7 Arctic/Antarctic repurchase,
  # itself UNVERIFIED); (iii) the default for a row the sources do not move is
  # its prior state (owned, on-curve). The call rests on (i) and (iii).
  # EXPOSURE if wrong, bounded: the two marks at 20.35/20.45y on the txn-anchored
  # Suezmax curve are about $61M = about $2.0/sh (base curve about $67M); the
  # 20-F carrying basis is smaller (repurchased Jul-19/Aug-22-2024 at $21,000K
  # each net of the $5,900K seller's credit; finance-lease liability remeasured
  # $43,316K incl. the $11,800K credit — 20-F leases note). FLIPS on a 6-K
  # vessels-held-for-sale note dating an MOA on or before 2026-06-30: rows OUT,
  # carrying value inside the WC composite (Other assets 286,240 already carries
  # it in that case), held_for_sale stays 0 — keeping them on-curve THEN would
  # double-count (verifier finding 2, decisions/ten_h1_release_check_2026-09-10.md).
